# Marks a link by what it leads to - another site, a file, an email address,
# a phone number - with a class, a glyph after its text and, for a new window
# or a download, a hint for a screen reader.
#
# The marking is done by a PSR-14 listener for every link TYPO3 builds from a
# link reference ("Classes/EventListener/LinkDecoration.php"), and a listener
# is registered for every site of an installation. This line is how it knows
# the page is one the theme renders: it acts only where "config." carries it.
# "config." rather than a key of the theme's own, because the listener reads
# the "config." of the request - the one part of the setup every page
# rendering sets up - and "tx_theme" keeps the key in the theme's namespace,
# the way "config.tx_extbase" is Extbase's.
#
# Switched by the constant "theme.linkDecoration"; "0" leaves every link as
# TYPO3 builds it.
config.tx_theme.linkDecoration = {$theme.linkDecoration}
